{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.32, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 10936, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1049, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01RhjfYCkHD5ECfUCFDgPK9n", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses the one-sided threshold: 2[ln L_max − ln L(<σv>_95)] = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, or 1.355 in ln L). The nuisance parameter it profiles is each dwarf's J-factor, written J = sJ0 with a Gaussian prior on log10 s (width σ_J, range log10 s in [−3, 3]). The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = 3.84 (Q = −2 ln L), taking the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region. The paper says this is the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold and differs from the usual one-sided 2.71. The nuisance parameter it profiles is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L. It has a Gaussian penalty in log10 L with L̂ = 4.96 kpc and σ = 0.197, over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T075357Z_dev-02_staged_6768", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The dSph gamma-ray limit uses the one-sided threshold: 2[ln L_max − ln L(<σv>_95)] = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, or 1.355 in ln L). The nuisance parameter it profiles is each dwarf's J-factor, written J = sJ0 with a Gaussian prior on log10 s (width σ_J, range log10 s in [−3, 3]). The AMS-02 antiproton limit uses ΔQ = 3.84 (Q = −2 ln L), taking the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region. The paper says this is the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold and differs from the usual one-sided 2.71. The nuisance parameter it profiles is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L. It has a Gaussian penalty in log10 L with L̂ = 4.96 kpc and σ = 0.197, over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 11.386, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19377, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1369, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25367, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T07:54:09+00:00"}
